# CLCA Protocol v3.4 — P2a Derivational System
# Language: {{ lang.name }} ({{ lang.code }})

# CONTEXT: P1 output (base lexical items)
{{ context }}

# TASK

Identify and document **attested derivational morphology**
associated with the lexical items identified in P1.

- Include only forms that are genuinely used or strongly supported in the language
- The number and type of derivations may vary by root
- If no derivation exists, explicitly state:
  (no common derivation identified)

---

## For each derived form provide:

1. Base Form (from P1)
2. Derived Form
3. Transliteration (consistent with P1)
4. Literal Breakdown (if known)
5. Natural English translation
6. Usage description (1–2 sentences)
7. Epistemic status: [CORE], [MARGINAL], or [UNCERTAIN]

---

## Important Constraints

- Do NOT assume that all types of derivation exist
- Do NOT complete paradigms or generate expected forms
- Do NOT invent unattested derivations
- Do NOT group forms into predefined categories
- Preserve asymmetry and gaps

---

## Additional Guidance

- It is acceptable for:
  - some roots to have many derivations
  - some roots to have none
  - derivations to be uneven or irregular

- Notes on productivity may be included only if directly supported by usage
